{"duration_ms":0,"id":19,"kind":"llm","model":"claude-opus-5","name":"claude-code.turn.13","provider":"anthropic","response":{"content":[{"text":"Fixed and verified.\n\n**The bug:** `def add_section(title, sections=[])` — Python evaluates default arguments once, at function definition time. That single list was shared by every call that omitted `sections`. Compounding it, `build_report` called `add_section(title)` without passing `result`, so it discarded its own empty list each iteration and returned the shared default instead. First call looked correct only because the shared list happened to start empty.\n\n**The fix** (`report.py:1-14`): use `None` as the sentinel and allocate a fresh list inside the function, and have `build_report` pass its accumulator explicitly so it builds its own list rather than depending on the default.\n\nRepeated calls are now independent (`['Intro', 'Body']` then `['Summary']`), an empty input returns `[]`, and `add_section` still works both standalone and with an explicit accumulator.","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011CeuAmyT9EtyacGvLbX3PP","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":17610,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"}},"start_ms":0,"usage":{"cache_read":17610,"cache_write_1h":287,"input":2,"output":5}}
